IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-8.l4 -- ARTICLE 8: A CHILD'S CONSENT IN RELATION TO INFORMATION SOCIETY SERVICES.  Layer 1 (P1).
-- "Child" is not defined in the Regulation and "information society service" is Art 4(25) (K2): both are
-- carried by plain input facts (`the offer ... is directly to a child`).  The child's age is a NUMBER of
-- complete years.  Whose duty: 8(1) a condition on the controller's processing and on whoever holds
-- parental responsibility (who may give or authorise consent); 8(2) the controller; 8(3) none.
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 8(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 8(2) make reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility`

§ `Article 8(1): the ages`

-- src:115 | 1. Where point (a) of Article 6(1) applies, in relation to the offer of information society services directly to a child, the processing of the personal data of a child shall be lawful where the child is at least 16 years old. Where the child is below the age of 16 years, such processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child.
@ref Art 8(1), first subparagraph (src:115)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 8(1) the age from which a child may consent unless a Member State has provided otherwise` MEANS 16

-- src:116 | Member States may provide by law for a lower age for those purposes provided that such lower age is not below 13 years.
@ref Art 8(1), second subparagraph (src:116)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 8(1) the lowest age a Member State may provide by law` MEANS 13

-- src:116 | Member States may provide by law for a lower age for those purposes provided that such lower age is not below 13 years.
@ref Art 8(1), second subparagraph (src:116)
GIVEN `the lower age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(1) a Member State may provide by law for the lower age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the lower age` LESS THAN `Art 8(1) the lowest age a Member State may provide by law`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "provided that"): "provided that such lower age is not below 13 years"; the function is named for a grant ("Member States may provide"), so fork F8-1 in NOTES.md records the other reading, NOTHING (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1), and split site (ii) lists it
        IF `the lower age` LESS THAN `Art 8(1) the age from which a child may consent unless a Member State has provided otherwise`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "a lower age"; an age of 16 or more is not lower than 16

-- src:115 | 1. Where point (a) of Article 6(1) applies, in relation to the offer of information society services directly to a child, the processing of the personal data of a child shall be lawful where the child is at least 16 years old. Where the child is below the age of 16 years, such processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child.
-- src:116 | Member States may provide by law for a lower age for those purposes provided that such lower age is not below 13 years.
@ref Art 8(1) (src:115-116)
GIVEN `the age a Member State has provided by law` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Art 8(1) the age from which the child may consent in this Member State` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the age a Member State has provided by law`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Art 8(1) the age from which a child may consent unless a Member State has provided otherwise`
    WHEN JUST age THEN
        IF `Art 8(1) a Member State may provide by law for the lower age` age EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN age
        ELSE `Art 8(1) the age from which a child may consent unless a Member State has provided otherwise`
    -- a provision of a Member State that sets an age the text does not allow (below 13, or not lower than 16) is read as not changing the age of 16 (fork F8-1 in NOTES.md)

-- src:115 | 1. Where point (a) of Article 6(1) applies, in relation to the offer of information society services directly to a child, the processing of the personal data of a child shall be lawful where the child is at least 16 years old. Where the child is below the age of 16 years, such processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child.
@ref Art 8(1), the cases the Article speaks of (src:115)
GIVEN `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information society services are offered directly to a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of the child in complete years` IS A NUMBER
      `the age a Member State has provided by law` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(1) the case is one in which the consent of the holder of parental responsibility is needed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`point (a) of Article 6(1) applies`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "Where"): "Where point (a) of Article 6(1) applies" (periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05, taken literally; fork F8-5 in NOTES.md)
        IF NOT (`the information society services are offered directly to a child`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the offer of information society services directly to a child" has no gate word (periods ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; fork F8-5 in NOTES.md)
        IF `the age of the child in complete years` LESS THAN `Art 8(1) the age from which the child may consent in this Member State` `the age a Member State has provided by law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- "Where the child is below the age of 16 years, such processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "Where"): the requirement is stated only for "Where the child is below the age of 16 years"; at or above the age the paragraph says the processing "shall be lawful where the child is at least 16 years old", so consent of the holder of parental responsibility is not needed (periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05)
    -- the same arms as the decision function below, so that the two cannot answer differently on the same facts; Art 8(2) uses this answer as its gate

-- src:115 | 1. Where point (a) of Article 6(1) applies, in relation to the offer of information society services directly to a child, the processing of the personal data of a child shall be lawful where the child is at least 16 years old. Where the child is below the age of 16 years, such processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child.
@ref Art 8(1), first subparagraph (src:115)
GIVEN `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information society services are offered directly to a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of the child in complete years` IS A NUMBER
      `the age a Member State has provided by law` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(1) the processing of a child's personal data meets the condition of Art 8(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`point (a) of Article 6(1) applies`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "Where"): "Where point (a) of Article 6(1) applies" (periods ruling (b) of 2026-11-05, taken literally; fork F8-5 in NOTES.md)
        IF NOT (`the information society services are offered directly to a child`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the offer of information society services directly to a child" has no gate word (periods ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; fork F8-5 in NOTES.md)
        IF `the age of the child in complete years` AT LEAST `Art 8(1) the age from which the child may consent in this Member State` `the age a Member State has provided by law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- "the processing of the personal data of a child shall be lawful where the child is at least 16 years old"
        IF `consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- below the age: "lawful only if and to the extent that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child" (the condition is met; it is not said to be sufficient)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only if"): "Where the child is below the age of 16 years, such processing shall be lawful only if and to the extent that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child."

§ `Article 8(2): verification`

-- src:117 | 2. The controller shall make reasonable efforts to verify in such cases that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child, taking into consideration available technology.
@ref Art 8(2) (src:117)
GIVEN `the case is one in which Art 8(1) requires the consent of the holder of parental responsibility` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the controller has made reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller took available technology into consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 8(2) the controller makes reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised, taking available technology into consideration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the case is one in which Art 8(1) requires the consent of the holder of parental responsibility` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in such cases" points back to the cases of Art 8(1) in which consent must be given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility; it is a scope pointer with no gate word, the same phrase that Art 11(2) second sentence reads as a scope limit (periods ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; forks F8-4 and F11-1 in NOTES.md, the other reading is `the duty does not arise`)
        IF `the controller has made reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility`
           AND `the controller took available technology into consideration`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "The controller shall make reasonable efforts to verify in such cases that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility over the child, taking into consideration available technology."

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: no time limit, no consequence (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
@ref Art 8(2), regulative form (src:117-117)
GIVEN `the case is one in which Art 8(1) requires the consent of the holder of parental responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 8(2) action`
`Art 8(2) the controller must make reasonable efforts to verify` MEANS
    IF `the case is one in which Art 8(1) requires the consent of the holder of parental responsibility`
    THEN PARTY `controller`
         MUST `Art 8(2) make reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `Art 8(2) the controller must make reasonable efforts to verify` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 8(2) make reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility` AT 2
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `Art 8(2) the controller must make reasonable efforts to verify` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: the obligation is still standing (no deadline, so no breach).

§ `Article 8(3): general contract law`

DECLARE `Art 8(3) what the rule of contract law concerns` IS ONE OF
    `Art 8(3) the validity of a contract in relation to a child`
    `Art 8(3) the formation of a contract in relation to a child`
    `Art 8(3) the effect of a contract in relation to a child`
    `Art 8(3) another rule of general contract law`

-- src:118 | 3. Paragraph 1 shall not affect the general contract law of Member States such as the rules on the validity, formation or effect of a contract in relation to a child.
@ref Art 8(3) (src:118)
GIVEN `the rule is part of the general contract law of a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the rule concerns` IS AN `Art 8(3) what the rule of contract law concerns`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 8(3) paragraph 1 affects the rule of the general contract law of a Member State` MEANS
    IF `the rule is part of the general contract law of a Member State`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative): "Paragraph 1 shall not affect the general contract law of Member States such as the rules on the validity, formation or effect of a contract in relation to a child."
    -- "such as ...": the three named rules are examples of "the general contract law"; `what the rule concerns` is not read.
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only "the general contract law of Member States" is spoken of
